  <div class="sections">
    <section class="section" id="firm"><h2>1. Firm information and registration</h2><p>Investment advisory services are provided through <strong>RIPL Wealth, LLC</strong>, an investment adviser registered with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. Registration does not imply a particular level of skill or training, and neither the SEC nor any state securities authority has approved this website or endorsed RIPL's services.</p><p>Advisory services are provided only under an appropriate agreement and where RIPL and its investment adviser representatives are appropriately registered, notice-filed, or exempt from applicable requirements. References to RIPL, “we,” or “our” on this page mean RIPL Wealth, LLC unless context indicates otherwise.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="regulatory"><h2>2. Regulatory documents and additional information</h2><p>Prospective clients should review RIPL's current Form ADV Part 2A brochure, applicable brochure supplements, Form CRS relationship summary (if applicable), and advisory agreement for detailed information about services, fees, methods of analysis, disciplinary information, and material conflicts of interest.</p><p><strong>Official regulatory source:</strong> <a href="https://adviserinfo.sec.gov/firm/summary/342258" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC Investment Adviser Public Disclosure (IAPD) — RIPL Wealth (CRD 342258)</a>. If the direct profile does not load, visit <a href="https://adviserinfo.sec.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adviserinfo.sec.gov</a> and search for RIPL Wealth or CRD 342258. Copies of current disclosure documents may also be requested directly from RIPL.</p><p>Information in regulatory filings and agreements controls in the event of a difference between those documents and this website.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="education"><h2>3. General educational information; no individual advice</h2><p>Articles, videos, examples, charts, quizzes, commentary, and other website content are provided for informational and educational purposes. They are not individualized investment, financial, tax, accounting, or legal advice and do not constitute an offer or solicitation to buy or sell any security or financial product.</p><p>Information may be simplified, may become outdated, and may not reflect all relevant facts or risks. Visitors should not make financial decisions based solely on this website. A formal advisory relationship does not arise from browsing the website, completing a quiz, submitting a question, or scheduling an introductory meeting.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="risks"><h2>4. Investment risks and limitations</h2><p>All investing involves risk, including the possible loss of principal. Securities and strategies may be affected by market volatility, changes in interest rates, inflation, credit conditions, liquidity constraints, tax-law changes, and other factors. Diversification, asset allocation, rebalancing, and risk-management techniques do not ensure a profit or prevent loss.</p><p>Different assets and strategies have different risks. Concentrated positions, small-capitalization securities, fixed-income securities, alternative investments, derivatives, and illiquid investments can carry additional or substantial risks. Past performance is not indicative of future results. No strategy is appropriate for every investor.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="fees"><h2>5. Advisory fees, expenses, and conflicts of interest</h2><p>RIPL may charge asset-based advisory fees and/or other fees for services as described in its current Form ADV and applicable client agreement. Actual charges depend on the services and terms agreed upon. Investments may also incur underlying fund expenses, trading costs, custody or account fees, taxes, and other third-party charges. Fees and expenses reduce investment returns.</p><p>Financial advisers and service providers can have financial or other incentives that create conflicts of interest, including incentives associated with the type or amount of assets managed, recommended services, third-party arrangements, or investment products. Material conflicts and the firm's policies for addressing them are described in its applicable disclosure documents. Clients should review these documents and ask questions before engaging RIPL.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="tax"><h2>6. Tax-aware planning and professional coordination</h2><p>Tax-aware investment strategies may help some investors manage the timing and character of taxable events, but tax outcomes are not guaranteed. The effectiveness of any approach depends on personal circumstances, account type, tax basis, holding periods, tax rates, market activity, and applicable law. Tax rules may change.</p><p>RIPL does not replace a client's CPA, attorney, or other licensed professional. References to coordinating with tax, estate, insurance, or legal professionals describe a collaborative planning approach, not a guarantee of a particular outcome or an assumption of those professionals' responsibilities. Consult appropriately qualified tax and legal advisers about your situation.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="direct-indexing"><h2>7. Direct indexing and tax-loss harvesting</h2><p>Direct indexing typically involves owning individual securities to pursue an index-like investment exposure, sometimes with tax-management features. Tax-loss harvesting may generate realized losses that could be useful under applicable tax rules, but benefits depend on the investor's tax circumstances and may be limited by wash-sale rules, gains, transaction costs, and other factors.</p><p>Direct indexing can produce tracking error relative to a benchmark, higher turnover, additional complexity, and different results from an index fund. Tax-management decisions may conflict with other investment objectives. No specific tax savings or outperformance is assured.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="notes"><h2>8. Structured notes and other complex investments</h2><p>Structured notes are debt obligations of an issuing financial institution whose payment terms are linked to one or more reference assets, indexes, or formulas. Their features and risks vary substantially. Potential risks include loss of some or all invested principal, issuer and guarantor credit risk, limited liquidity, unfavorable secondary-market pricing, complex payoff conditions, caps on participation, early redemption or call features, and potentially unfavorable tax treatment.</p><p>References to buffers, barriers, contingent coupons, income, or principal protection are product-specific and subject to the applicable terms, conditions, and creditworthiness of the issuer. “Principal-protected” does not mean free of risk and generally depends on holding the note to maturity and the issuer's ability to pay. Investors should read the applicable offering documents and discuss risks, fees, and alternatives before investing.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="income"><h2>9. Income illustrations, projections, and examples</h2><p>Any investment examples, projected values, assumed rates, distributions, or hypothetical scenarios appearing in RIPL materials are illustrative unless expressly identified otherwise. They may rely on assumptions that do not occur in practice, and actual results may differ materially. Illustrations do not represent a promise of future performance.</p><p>Cash distributions, coupons, or dividends are not equivalent to total investment return and may be accompanied by losses in principal value. Some distributions may include a return of capital. Taxes, fees, expenses, reinvestment assumptions, and liquidity constraints may materially affect actual results. Specific performance presentations, if any, are subject to additional disclosures accompanying those presentations.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="quiz"><h2>10. Quiz, assessment, and introductory meetings</h2><p>Any “Lazy Money Quiz,” business-owner assessment, or similar tool is intended to prompt useful questions and educational discussion. Results may be generated from general rules and the answers provided, rather than a comprehensive review of financial documents. Quiz outputs are not a financial plan, an investment recommendation, a determination of suitability, or a guarantee that a particular financial issue exists.</p><p>A complimentary introductory call is a discussion to explore questions and whether further work may be appropriate. It is not a promise of a complete financial, tax, or investment analysis. Any paid service, if offered, will have separately described terms and scope.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="third-parties"><h2>11. External links, custodians, and third-party services</h2><p>This website may link to or embed third-party sites and services, including scheduling tools, video hosts, analytics providers, custodians, and educational resources. Those third parties have their own terms, privacy practices, and security controls. A link or reference does not by itself imply endorsement, affiliation, or a guarantee of accuracy.</p><p>Client assets, when held at an independent custodian, remain subject to the terms, protections, and risks applicable to that custodian and account. FDIC insurance and SIPC protection, where applicable, have eligibility conditions and limits and do not protect investors against ordinary market losses. Any specific coverage claim should be verified against current program documents.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="privacy"><h2>12. Privacy, communications, and information security</h2><p>Website interactions and third-party tools may process technical information and, where submitted, contact details or quiz responses. For information about this landing page's practices, please review our <a href="/money-at-work-privacy/">Privacy Notice</a>. Other firm privacy notices or policies may apply to established client relationships.</p><p>Do not submit Social Security numbers, tax returns, account credentials, account statements, or other highly sensitive documents through ordinary website forms, unsecured email, or quiz fields. No internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Request a firm-approved secure channel when sharing confidential information.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="geography"><h2>13. Geographic and legal limitations</h2><p>This website may be accessible from jurisdictions in which RIPL or its representatives are not registered or permitted to provide investment advisory services. Availability of services is subject to applicable federal and state law. The website is not intended as a solicitation in any jurisdiction where such solicitation would be unlawful.</p><p>RIPL may update or correct website information without notice. If a provision of this page conflicts with a current executed advisory agreement or required regulatory document, the applicable agreement or regulatory document governs.</p></section>
